Challenge Description
In this write-up, we are going to tackle the Sql Map1 challenge from picoCTF. The premise is a “Vulnerable Flag Search” page. But as the description hints, we aren’t just looking for an injection flaw — we have to exploit “legacy hashing practices” to act as a legitimate user.

Approach
The challenge presents a web application with one or more user-input fields that are vulnerable to ‘SQL injection’. The name “Sql Map1” strongly hints that the intended solution path is to use sqlmap,Here is how we went from a basic search box to dumping a database and cracking MD5 hashes to get the final flag.

Step 1 — Launch the Challenge Instance
Open the provided link in Challenge page. Resgister there with dummy credential then login. After login you will get a search page.

